.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt OTELCONF 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm otelconf
.Nd validate and query the system OpenTelemetry configuration
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl d Ar defaults
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Cm check
.Op Fl eqt
.Nm
.Op Fl d Ar defaults
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Cm show
.Nm
.Op Fl d Ar defaults
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Cm get
.Ar key
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
loads
.Xr otel.conf 5
with the same code and checks that the base exporter library uses, so
a configuration it accepts is accepted by every telemetry program.
.Pp
The global options select other files than
.Pa /etc/defaults/otel.conf
.Pq Fl d
and
.Pa /etc/otel.conf
.Pq Fl f .
A path that does not exist contributes nothing.
.Pp
The commands are:
.Bl -tag -width "check"
.It Cm check Op Fl eqt
Load and validate both files and the exporter credentials file.
Prints
.Dq otel.conf: OK ,
noting a disabled configuration or a missing export target, unless
.Fl q
is given; errors are always reported.
With
.Fl e ,
also fail with exit status 3 when
.Ic enable
is false.
With
.Fl t ,
also fail with exit status 4 when the configuration names no export
target
.Po
.Ic endpoint ,
a signal block's
.Ic endpoint ,
or
.Ic export.target
.Qq file
.Pc
for the base system services.
The rc.d services use
.Fl eqt .
.It Cm show
Print every resolved setting, and the settings the signal blocks
.Pq Ic logs , metrics , traces , profiles
set.
Header values are redacted.
.It Cm get Ar key
Print one resolved setting.
.Ar key
is a key of
.Xr otel.conf 5
written with dots, such as
.Cm endpoint ,
.Cm spool.directory ,
.Cm export.target
or
.Cm traces.endpoint .
A signal block key that the block does not set prints an empty line:
the general key applies.
The list-valued key
.Cm resource
prints one entry per line.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
Usage errors and unknown keys exit 2; a disabled configuration exits 3
for
.Cm check Fl e ,
and a configuration without an export target exits 4 for
.Cm check Fl t .
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ otelconf check
otel.conf: OK (no export target)
# echo 'endpoint = "https://collector.example.org:4318";' >> /etc/otel.conf
# otelconf check -t
otel.conf: OK
$ otelconf get endpoint
https://collector.example.org:4318
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr oe_sysconf 3 ,
.Xr otel.conf 5 ,
.Xr rc.conf 5
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in 5BSD.
